# Signing material. The patterns below are anchored at docs/ and do NOT reach
# subdirectories, so docs/key/ (p12 private keys, CSRs and the keystore
# material tree) needs its own rule -- without it a `git add -A` would publish
# the app signing keys to a public repository.
docs/key/
docs/*.csr
docs/*.p12
docs/*.p7b
# Belt and braces: never commit key material from anywhere in the tree.
**/*.p12
**/*.csr
**/*.p7b
**/*.keystore
**/*.cer
# DevEco keystore material trees (hash-bucketed ac/ce/fd directories).
# NOTE: docs/material/ was already tracked before this rule existed (committed in
# bc19b09) and .gitignore does not untrack anything -- see docs/handoff.md,
# "2026-07-28 Tracked Signing Material". This rule only stops NEW material dirs.
docs/material/
docs/key/material/
third_party/libssh2/
third_party/mbedtls/
